stateDiagram-v2
    accTitle: Settings module lifecycle
    accDescr: A module starts Discovered when its manifest is found. The manifest is signature-verified; failure moves it to Rejected and nothing else happens. On success the loader checks the requested capabilities against policy, then admits its definitions into the registry (Active). Deactivation or removal returns it to Discovered or unloads it entirely.
    [*] --> Discovered
    Discovered --> VerifySignature
    VerifySignature --> Rejected: invalid signature
    VerifySignature --> CheckPolicy: valid signature
    CheckPolicy --> Rejected: capability not allowed
    CheckPolicy --> Active: allowed
    Active --> RegistryLoaded: definitions merged
    RegistryLoaded --> Active
    Active --> Unloaded: removed by user/policy
    Unloaded --> [*]
    Rejected --> [*]
